# Cline Rules — see CLAUDE.md

> **This file is intentionally a pointer, not a rulebook.**
>
> Ops Agenda keeps a single source of truth for AI-assistant behaviour so the
> rules cannot drift between tools. Previously this file duplicated ~300 lines
> that already existed elsewhere; those copies had begun to disagree with each
> other.

## Read these instead, in order

1. **[CLAUDE.md](CLAUDE.md)** — project overview, identity, tech stack,
   tooling preferences, and the memory-bank system.
2. **[setup/docs/AGENT_HANDBOOK.md](setup/docs/AGENT_HANDBOOK.md)** — source of
   truth for operating principles, intake questions, architecture boundaries,
   the quality bar, and security/privacy rules.
3. **[setup/docs/WORKFLOW.md](setup/docs/WORKFLOW.md)** — the five phases:
   Discovery → Planning → Implementation → Verification → Release Readiness.
4. **[TECHSTACK.md](TECHSTACK.md)** — locked technology decisions.

## Non-negotiables (summary only — the handbook governs)

- Start in plan mode; ask the required intake questions; wait for answers.
- Never speculate about code you have not opened.
- No raw email bodies stored — metadata and AI summaries only.
- No autonomous actions — AI suggests, the user approves.
- JSON-only AI output, schema-validated on every response.
- Least-privilege Graph scopes: `Mail.Read`, `Calendars.Read`.
- Conventional Commits for every commit.

*Superseded copy archived at `_archive/ai-rules-consolidated-2026-07-30/`.*
